# Line endings, pinned so that a file built on Windows is byte-identical to the same file
# built on the Linux CI runner. Without this the Pages workflow's "is the committed data
# current?" check fails on every run: it rebuilds the outputs and diffs them, and a file
# whose endings changed on checkout differs on every single line.

# Default: LF in the repository and LF on checkout, everywhere, for everyone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Exception. scripts/build.mjs writes exports/terms.csv with a UTF-8 BOM and CRLF endings
# on purpose — that combination is what Excel needs to open a CSV full of Chinese without
# mangling it, and this file exists to be handed to a native-speaker reviewer. Forcing
# CRLF on checkout keeps the build reproducible without giving up the Excel behaviour.
# The blob in the repository stays LF either way; only the working copy is affected.
exports/*.csv text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touch these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.zip binary
